Direction: representation

Effect: An entry's slots are its modifier positions in syntax order; `optional` slots may be
  omitted. The mask of a slot has bit `Slot.code s t` set for every choice `t`. An operand's lanes
  (number of registers), type token and whether a lane may be the sink `_` are `Fact`s: a constant,
  the token of a slot, or a table keyed by the codes of the slots the fact depends on (base-128
  digits in slot order). The effect class is `event` for an entry with an address operand or one
  that orders memory, `ctl` for control flow and `local` otherwise. Excluded table entries (wgmma)
  have no constructor. A table entry whose PTX spelling is that of another entry (mapa with a
  pointer or an integer address; the `.b8` and `.b16` TMA override tensor sizes) has no constructor
  either and decodes as that entry (`ALIASES` in `Tools/isa/families.py`); an operand whose type
  differs between the two has no type token. Corrections of the table: `elect.sync`'s `d` may be the
  sink, and every `tcgen05.mma` entry with a `disable-output-lane` vector has a sibling
  `<name>_nomask` without it, the form of the ISA's examples. `mapa` is split by its `.space`
  qualifier: `mapa` (with `.shared::cluster`) takes a variable `var` or `var+imm` as `a`, and
  `mapa_generic` (without `.space`) takes a register. `getctarank` takes a variable as `a`; `mov`'s
  `a` may be a variable with an offset (`regvar`); `ld` and `ld_vec` accept the `.const` space.
